content:
{
  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "Primary objective wording is contradictory: compares OS for patients with SCC and 'any eligible histology' but then specifies only SCC",
      "page": 37,
      "quote": "To compare OS for patients with recurrent or metastatic cervical cancer who have histology of squamous cell carcinoma (SCC) and who have any eligible histology, treated with either cemiplimab or investigator’s choice (IC) chemotherapy.",
      "severity": "critical"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent enrollment numbers: Section 3.2.1 says total enrollment approximately 590 and 80% squamous, but Section 6.1 says approximately 460 SCC patients and approximately 590 overall, which implies 78% squamous, not 80%",
      "page": 40,
      "quote": "total enrollment to the study will be approximately 590 patients, and approximately 80% of patients will have squamous histology.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent total OS events: Section 5.2 says first interim at 238 events (70% of total) and second at 289 events (85% of total), but 238/0.70 = 340 and 289/0.85 = 340, so total events is 340, but Section 5.1.2 says approximately 340 deaths in squamous patients, not overall",
      "page": 46,
      "quote": "The end of study for the study as a whole is planned to occur when approximately 340 deaths have occurred in squamous cell patients, as per Section 10.2.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Cross-reference error: Section 5.1.2 refers to 'Section Section 7.1.7' (duplicate 'Section')",
      "page": 46,
      "quote": "a cemiplimab Extension Phase was added (Section Section 7.1.7).",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent topotecan dose: Section 3.2.3 says starting dose is 1 mg/m2 per day for 5 consecutive days, but Figure 2 shows topotecan 1.0 mg/m2 on Days 1-5 (Q3W) - consistent, but Section 3.2.3 also mentions a phase 2 study with 1.5 mg/m2 and says 'the starting topotecan dose and schedule in this protocol is 1 mg/m2 per day for 5 consecutive days' - no contradiction, but the protocol does not specify dose modifications for topotecan, which is a missing information",
      "page": 41,
      "quote": "the starting topotecan dose and schedule in this protocol is 1 mg/m2 per day for 5 consecutive days",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent gemcitabine exposure calculation: Section 3.2.3 says over 12 weeks, 21-day course provides 8000 mg vs 7200 mg for 28-day course, but 1000 mg/m2 on days 1 and 8 of a 21-day cycle for 4 cycles (12 weeks) gives 8000 mg/m2, not 8000 mg; the comparison is flawed because it ignores body surface area",
      "page": 41,
      "quote": "Over 12 weeks, this 21-day treatment course provides similar exposure to gemcitabine (8000 mg) as the 28-day treatment course in the Schilder study (7200 mg).",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent statement about prior paclitaxel and bevacizumab: Section 3.2.1 says 'The study population will have received prior paclitaxel and prior bevacizumab, refused such treatment, or been unsuitable for such treatment', but inclusion criteria do not mention prior paclitaxel or bevacizumab requirement",
      "page": 39,
      "quote": "The study population will have received prior paclitaxel and prior bevacizumab, refused such treatment, or been unsuitable for such treatment (or, in the case of bevacizumab, not had access).",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent statement about histology: Section 3.2.1 says 'enrollment will only be allowed for patients with squamous histology' but Section 6.2.1 inclusion criterion 1 says 'with squamous cell histology' and also mentions acceptable histologies from original protocol through Amendment 4, which is fine, but Section 2.1 primary objective says 'any eligible histology' which is contradictory",
      "page": 40,
      "quote": "enrollment will only be allowed for patients with squamous histology",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Missing information: The protocol does not specify the randomization ratio in Section 5.1 (it says approximately 590 patients will be randomized but does not state 1:1 ratio, though Figure 2 shows 1:1)",
      "page": 44,
      "quote": "Approximately 590 patients will be randomized to either the experimental cemiplimab treatment arm or the IC of chemotherapy control treatment arm.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent statement about treatment duration: Section 5.1 says 'Planned treatment is for up to 96 weeks' and Figure 2 says 'until 96 weeks (16cycles, each 6 weeks)' but Section 5.1.2 says 'end of study for the study as a whole is planned to occur when approximately 340 deaths have occurred in squamous cell patients' - no contradiction, but the protocol does not specify what happens after 96 weeks for patients still on treatment",
      "page": 46,
      "quote": "Planned treatment is for up to 96 weeks.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent statement about follow-up: Section 5.1 says 'After the follow-up period, patients will be followed for survival' but Section 5.1.2 says 'end of study occurs for each individual patient after the patient completes or discontinues from the treatment (Table 1) and/or follow-up visit 1 and 2 portion of Table 2, but before the survival follow-up portion of Table 2' - this is contradictory because survival follow-up is part of follow-up period",
      "page": 46,
      "quote": "After the follow-up period, patients will be followed for survival.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent statement about interim analyses: Section 5.2 says 'Two interim efficacy analyses are planned' but Section 5.1.2 mentions 'second interim analysis' and 'cemiplimab Extension Phase' - no contradiction, but the protocol does not specify the timing of the second interim analysis relative to the extension phase",
      "page": 46,
      "quote": "Due to survival benefit, for patients on the cemiplimab arm on second interim analysis, a cemiplimab Extension Phase was added",
      "severity": "minor"
    }
  ]
}
